      "writtenOn": "2026-01-12T13:58:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The minifying code is, uh, quite something. The Skia team ended up doing the in-line string minifying for Ganesh and I haven\u0027t heard too many complaints about it, but probably because that code isn\u0027t very active.\nFor the more recent Graphite code, we built a build-step phase that piped the uniminified shaders (which were in their own files) into `skslc` which could minify them properly (including shortened variable names) and then had our release code include the minified versions instead of the unminified versions that debug included.\n\nThat might be a better approach if we wanted an automated minifying approach.",
      "parentUuid": "fde4dd97_28d51ed2",
      "revId": "cf5555c06f5eff08bfc9e561f1d2f54ec15f8f45",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
